<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.9.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01413</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.9.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>29109296-33cd-4d17-97c7-0c5881ef6160</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="aaebd88e-722e-41ba-998e-09e3de2f2070" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
  <!--q1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="61773217-5b27-4b8b-bfca-abc27475c09f" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="50">
    <problem>
      <para> The number of people with the flu during an epidemic is a function, \(f\), of the number of days, \(d\), since the epidemic began. The equation \(f(d)=50 \cdot (\frac{3}{2})^d\) defines \(f\).
          <para> How many people had the flu at the beginning of the epidemic? Do not enter commas or spaces in your answer.</para>
          </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.9.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="8f49e66b-5a03-4b16-99ef-0d156a165ea6" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="The number of people infected 1 day after the epidemic began." data-solution-options="[&quot;There was 1 year of the epidemic.&quot;, &quot;The number of people infected 1 day after the epidemic began.&quot;, &quot;The number of people infected grows by a factor of 1.&quot;, &quot;The number of people infected after 1 year.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>What does \(f(1)\) mean in this situation? </para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.9.2. 
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="88f841b1-5c27-4127-a0e9-d2f11e8db5c5" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="1000">
    <problem>
      <para>The function, \(f\)<emphasis>,</emphasis> gives the dollar value of a bond \(t\) years after the bond was purchased. The graph of \(f\) is shown.
          <para><figure><media alt="Graph of function."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/2269474d29cf53c5577e273f7d4b2c88beabe604"/></media></figure></para>
        </para>
        <para>What is \(f(0)\)? Do not enter commas or spaces in your answer. </para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 5.9.2.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="d38e53c0-9f96-4884-a292-16de37669801" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="8">
    <problem>
      <para>When is \(f(t)=1500\)? Estimate the nearest whole number. Do not enter commas or spaces in your answer.
          </para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 5.9.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--3a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="aa87cef9-a6e1-47db-8e21-1aab28675ffa" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="243">
    <problem>
      <para>A function \(f\) gives the number of stray cats in a town \(t\) years since the town started an animal control program. The program includes both sterilizing stray cats and finding homes to adopt them. An equation representing \(f\) is \(f(t)=243{(\frac13)}^t\).</para>
        <para> What is the value of \(f(t)\) when \(t\) is 0?
          </para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 5.9.2 – 5.9.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--3b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="577e38c4-c993-4814-8eae-e434b4ce5220" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="81">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the value of \(f(t)\) when \(t\) is 1? </para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 5.9.2 – 5.9.3. 
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--4a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="4f5580f5-59be-4273-862f-60c80bd2e0ee" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(t\geq0\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(t\\geq0\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(t\\geq600\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(t\\leq600\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(0\\leq t\\leq600\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Function \(g\) gives the amount of a chemical in a person’s body, in milligrams, \(t\) hours since the patient took the drug. The equation \(g(t)=600\cdot (\frac35)^t\) defines this function.</para>
        <para>Which is the best choice for the domain of \(g\)?</para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 5.9.3.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--4b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="a44a2625-bc54-4d52-922f-2e0156f3ebe7" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(0 &lt; g \leq 600\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(g &gt; 0\\) &quot;, &quot;\\(g\\geq 600\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(g \\leq 600\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(0 &lt; g \\leq 600\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which is the best choice for the range of \(g\)? </para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 5.9.3.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution> </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> </div>
</div>
  </section>
